---
/* Lengths follow the client wiki: detox 5 to 7 days commercial / 3 days Medicaid;
   residential 25 to 30 days commercial / 30 to 45 days Medicaid. Note the inversion —
   Medicaid residential authorizations tend to run LONGER than commercial ones,
   which is worth stating plainly since most people assume the reverse. */
const factors = [
  { h: 'What you have been using', p: 'Alcohol detox commonly needs the longer end of the range, often close to a full week. Stimulants on their own usually skip the detox stage entirely and begin with residential care.' },
  { h: 'How your body responds', p: 'Withdrawal does not run to a timetable. Your clinical team watch how you are doing day by day and adjust rather than holding you to a number set on the first morning.' },
  { h: 'How much your insurance approves', p: 'Cover is approved in blocks, and residential is commonly approved around thirty days. AHCCCS plans often run longer than commercial ones, sometimes toward forty-five days, which surprises people who assume the reverse.' },
  { h: 'What you decide together', p: 'From early on, someone is working with you on what comes after. If more time would genuinely help, they will make that case; if you are ready sooner, they will say that too.' },
  { h: 'How far down the continuum you go', p: 'Detox and residential are the start of it. PHP and IOP step the hours down, and outpatient treatment typically runs 45 to 90 days, sometimes more. End to end that is usually around 90 to 120 days.' },
  { h: 'Where you will be living', p: 'The later phases assume somewhere steady to sleep. Many people pair them with a sober living home, and settling that early is often what decides whether the last stretch of treatment holds.' },
];
---
<section id="factors" class="bg-cream py-[60px]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-start">
      <div>
        <p class="text-gold font-body text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-px bg-gold inline-block"></span>
          What decides it
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal mb-6">What makes one stay longer than another</h2>
        <div class="space-y-5 font-body text-charcoal text-[17px] leading-[29px]">
          <p>
            The ranges on this page are real, but they are ranges for a reason. Two people arriving on the same day with the same substance can need quite different amounts of time, and pretending otherwise would just set you up for a surprise.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="font-bold">One thing worth knowing:</strong> if you are covered by an Access plan, your residential authorization will often be longer than a commercial policy would allow — the opposite of what most people expect.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8">
          <a href="tel:8883625576" class="bg-teal hover:bg-teal-dark text-white font-bold px-7 py-3.5 rounded-lg transition-colors font-body tracking-wide inline-block">
            Find out what yours would be
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        {factors.map(f => (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-7 border border-cream-soft shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="font-display text-[20px] leading-[26px] text-navy mb-3">{f.h}</h3>
            <p class="font-body text-charcoal text-[16px] leading-[26px]">{f.p}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
